# 🗣️ Communication Practice — 100–200 Words

### Topic: **A Project I Have Worked On**

When I explain a project in an interview, I focus on the problem, my solution, the technologies I used, and my specific contribution. I first explain why the project was needed and what problem it solves. Then I describe the main features without going too deeply into implementation details. After that, I explain the technology stack and why I selected those technologies. Most importantly, I clearly explain what I personally developed because interviewers want to understand my technical contribution. Finally, I discuss one challenge I faced and how I solved it. This structure makes the explanation organized and demonstrates both technical knowledge and problem-solving ability. I also prepare for follow-up questions because interviewers may ask why I selected a particular database, framework, or architecture.

### 🎤 Speaking task:

Explain **one of your projects in 90 seconds**:

**Problem → Solution → Tech Stack → Your Contribution → Challenge → Result**

